From 6c5e380dc312a986dce599302fb5637f98012549 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fountain5405 <Fountain5405@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:15:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/27] tests: a block with an invalid transaction the pool
 never accepted

gen_bad_tx_in_block mines a block of 8, 9, 16 or 17 transactions with
one defective transaction in the middle, submitted kept-by-block as on
a block's arrival, and checks that the block is refused whole: the
height is unchanged and the defective transaction is not in the chain.
The same block with that transaction replaced by a valid spend of the
same output is then accepted.

The defects are a bad BP+ proof, a key image outside the prime-order
subgroup, a broken balance, L and R swapped in the BP+ proof, and a
broken ring signature. The ring signature is the one defect the pool
stores without validating on this path, so there the block's own
verification is the first to see it. The sizes sit on and just above
the thresholds of the batched key-image checks (8) and the parallel
sum checks (16).

Twelve instances, about 3 min of core_tests time with the two files
that follow.

Written by the second reviewer; adopted here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
